    {
      "id": "e52yar6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Binary Arithmetic and Representation"
    },
    {
      "id": "07lumqc",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "1s Complement: invert all bits (0→1, 1→0)",
        "2s Complement: invert all bits + add 1; used for signed integer representation in computers",
        "For 8-bit signed: range is -128 to +127 (2s complement)",
        "For 8-bit unsigned: range is 0 to 255",
        "IEEE 754 Floating Point: sign (1 bit) + exponent + mantissa; single (32-bit), double (64-bit)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pvcwraj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.5 Pipelining"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h5n2ds0",
      "content": "Pipelining is a technique to increase CPU throughput by overlapping execution of multiple instructions. Like an assembly line — different stages of different instructions execute simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Memory Hierarchy ranking questions frequently test relative access speed, cost, and capacity across Registers, Cache, RAM, and Hard Drive.",
        "RISC vs CISC architectural differences, such as register usage, instruction length, and clock cycles per instruction, are repeatedly asked in competitive exams.",
        "Number System conversions and 1's/2's Complement representations form a major part of numerical problems."
      ],
      "id": "8all1e2"
    },
    {
      "id": "523cctp",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Concept</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Stages (typical)</p>",
            "<p>IF (Instruction Fetch) → ID (Decode) → EX (Execute) → MEM (Memory Access) → WB (Write Back)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Throughput</p>",
            "<p>Ideally 1 instruction per clock cycle (CPI = 1) with 5-stage pipeline</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pipeline Hazards</p>",
            "<p>Situations preventing next instruction from executing in next clock cycle</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Structural Hazard</p>",
            "<p>Hardware resource conflict; two instructions need same resource</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Data Hazard</p>",
            "<p>Instruction depends on result of previous instruction; RAW, WAR, WAW hazards</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Control Hazard</p>",
            "<p>Branch instruction; don't know next instruction until branch resolved</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hazard Solutions</p>",
            "<p>Stalling (pipeline bubble), Data forwarding, Branch prediction, Out-of-order execution</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Speedup</p>",
            "<p>Ideal speedup = k stages; limited by hazards and pipeline fill/drain time</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alowqsu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.6 RISC vs CISC"
    },
    {
      "id": "87w5e39",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>RISC (Reduced Instruction Set Computer)</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>CISC (Complex Instruction Set Computer)</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Instructions</p>",
            "<p>Simple, fixed-length; few addressing modes</p>",
            "<p>Complex, variable-length; many addressing modes</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Execution</p>",
            "<p>1 cycle per instruction (mostly)</p>",
            "<p>Multi-cycle instructions common</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pipeline</p>",
            "<p>Easy to pipeline; regular format</p>",
            "<p>Difficult to pipeline; variable format</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Registers</p>",
            "<p>Many general-purpose registers</p>",
            "<p>Fewer registers; memory-to-memory operations</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Memory Access</p>",
            "<p>Load-Store architecture only</p>",
            "<p>Can operate directly on memory</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Compiler</p>",
            "<p>Complex compiler needed</p>",
            "<p>Simpler assembly; complex hardware</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Examples</p>",
            "<p>ARM, MIPS, SPARC, RISC-V</p>",
            "<p>x86, x86-64 (Intel/AMD), VAX</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
